%% nearby_boot.glp --- declare(nearby(pan, S)) under :boot.
%
% GLP-Spec 210cee1, appendix-guards, "Networking seam": nearby(U, S) assigns
% S a stream of the agents nearby over the proximity underlay U, seen(K) when
% the layer discovers on U an agent of key K that it recognises or, under open
% trust, contacts, and gone(K) when that agent can no longer be reached over
% U; remove(nearby(U)) ends the declaration and closes its stream.  IGLP
% 45fabfc, Implementation Notes, "Simulation realisation": "A nearby
% declaration on the PAN is given seen for an adjacent agent the declaring
% agent has declared a peer, and for any other adjacent agent once the PAN
% trust levels of both are open"; the adjacency relation is total by
% default, so bob is adjacent to alice from the boot, and "the harness sets
% no trust level at spawn".  Alice knows bob: she declares him a peer,
% declare(peer(bob)), and a watch on the PAN at her start, tells her person
% the first presence it carries, then removes the declaration and tells her
% person that the stream is closed.  Section MB, MB8, runs it.
%
%% The agents' program is the program directory nearby/ beside this file,
%% which the agents load, this file carrying its boot clause and the persons
%% it names and nothing else (TGLP 6ce148a, modules.tex, "Entry and the
%% absence of a boot module"; IGLP, Implementation Notes, "Boot").

procedure boot.
boot :- agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice, say(alice, ch(_?, _))@alice, agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@bob, say(bob, ch(_?, _))@bob.

%% The person at each agent tells it its name, and reads nothing.
exported procedure say(Constant?, Channel(Stream(Constant), Stream(Constant))?).
say(P, ch(_, [P?])).
